            </note>
            <note corresp="#d921-f2" n="9" xml:id="d921-f2-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Infra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d921-f3" n="10" xml:id="d921-f3-content">
                <p>Prince Regent of Yugoslavia.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d921-f4" n="11" xml:id="d921-f4-content">
                <p>Vlada Maček, Yugoslav Vice President of the Council of Ministers, and President
                    of the Croatian Peasant Party.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d921-f5" n="12" xml:id="d921-f5-content">
                <p>William J. Donovan, personal representative of the Secretary of the Navy on
                    special mission in Europe.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d921-f6" n="13" xml:id="d921-f6-content">
                <p>For the Secretary’s statement, see Department of State <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bulletin</hi>, January 15, 1941, p. 85.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
